# External paths hooks may access outside the harness root, in addition
# to repos/ and worktree/. The value below is the shipped default and
# applies even without a .env — it is the single source of the default,
# so a user .env only ever adds entries on top. Comma or colon
# separated; supports a leading `~` for $HOME. There is no blanket
# "allow everything outside the harness root" switch.
#
# Hooks read .env.sample and .env from the checkout root AND the lab
# root (the directory holding repos/ + worktree/); all lists are
# combined. Put a single .env at the lab root to add paths for every
# checkout on the machine. Changes apply on the next tool call — the
# files are read per hook invocation.
ALLOWED_EXT_DIRS=/tmp,~/.claude,~/.codex,~/.config/devin,~/.gemini
